{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ac2cad0c-bd8e-473d-a7ab-592587e8db6b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8d287263d3ac714","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-_h9vt6_q/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: whether vLLM serving on AMD Instinct accelerators reaches functional and performance parity with the productized CUDA builds for our supported model set. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware and produces a per-model report with functional pass/fail results, performance measurements against the CUDA baseline, and a go/no-go recommendation that defines the productization scope. The platform currently ships only CUDA runtime builds and has no first-hand parity data, so this campaign is the gate for all serving productization work in this strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the validation plan: enumerate the supported model set and the functional and performance parity criteria to be measured for each model.\n- Obtain execution access to physical AMD Instinct GPU nodes (procurement or partner-lab access — see Risks).\n- Serve every model in the supported model set with the upstream vLLM ROCm runtime on AMD Instinct hardware.\n- Record functional results (correct inference behavior vs the CUDA baseline) and performance measurements (throughput and latency) per model.\n- Produce a validation report with a per-model go/no-go recommendation and the resulting productization scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A validation plan exists that enumerates the supported model set and defines the functional and performance parity criteria measured for each model.\n- Every model in the supported model set has been served with the vLLM ROCm runtime on physical AMD Instinct hardware and has a recorded functional pass/fail result against the CUDA baseline.\n- Every model in the supported model set has recorded performance measurements (throughput and latency) on AMD Instinct hardware alongside comparable CUDA-baseline numbers.\n- A validation report is published with a per-model go/no-go recommendation that defines the productization scope for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization — fully covered by this epic.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- **Hardware access is unresolved** (strategy open question): dedicated AMD Instinct nodes require procurement or partner-lab access. This is an externally-controlled availability precondition — the epic's deliverable is the validated report; securing access is effort within the epic, but the access being granted is not a condition the deliverable itself produces.\n- **Upstream ROCm image cadence** is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; the campaign consumes upstream ROCm builds and may need to re-run against newer images.\n- The campaign also exercises KServe InferenceService deployment behavior on AMD GPU nodes; findings feed the serving runtime productization scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44196,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91f30b115d6e219b","agent_id":"a5586881f516d3574","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"d892ee4e-c908-4e0b-9c3d-b692bde46a18","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:07:14.496Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
