{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-038f135f-3312-4ee4-80ac-f5fd9529b693","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be0e62069a1a2f4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-_h9vt6_q/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a supported, productized vLLM serving runtime built for AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm), covering the models the validation campaign clears. Today only CUDA (NVIDIA) builds of the vLLM runtime are productized; ROCm builds exist upstream but are neither shipped nor supported. This epic turns the cleared subset of the supported model set into a shipped, supported runtime for the platform.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build and release a ROCm variant of the vLLM serving runtime image in the existing midstream vLLM repository and release pipeline, scoped to the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n- Provide the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime definitions that expose the ROCm runtime variant for AMD GPU nodes.\n- Verify KServe InferenceService deployment with the ROCm runtime (KServe itself requires no code change — it is validated as a passive component by the same team).\n- Track upstream vLLM ROCm releases and pin to compatible upstream image versions per platform release (upstream cadence risk, see Risks).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A ROCm build of the vLLM serving runtime is produced and released through the platform release pipeline, scoped to the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n- The ROCm runtime image builds green in the Konflux build pipeline (the build-pipeline onboarding for this image runs in parallel with this epic; its coupling is enforced by this acceptance criterion, not by a dependency between the two work items).\n- Every model cleared by the validation campaign deploys and serves correctly via a KServe InferenceService using the ROCm runtime on AMD GPU nodes.\n- The runtime ships with a support statement identifying the cleared model set and the AMD hardware it is validated on.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the models the validation campaign clears — covered by this epic together with the Konflux build-pipeline work for the ROCm image (a work-product-type split: runtime productization vs. build-pipeline onboarding).\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- **Upstream ROCm build cadence** (strategy open question): whether AMD's runtime image releases align with our release trains is outside our control. If cadence misaligns, the runtime pins to or rebuilds from the nearest compatible upstream release — fix-and-retry, not a structural change.\n- The scope of this epic is rewritten (not merely trimmed) by the validation campaign outcome: the cleared model set defines what is productized and what the support statement covers.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44959,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91f30b115d6e219b","agent_id":"a5586881f516d3574","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"11a3f4f8-132a-43ba-bd33-dd535c78fa5d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:07:24.974Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
