{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b7e3c690-af8c-4e63-9107-9bb395496057","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab5d2bdac6cf8428","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-_h9vt6_q/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E004.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training enablement for PyTorchJob workloads\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic enables PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) for workloads run through the platform's Training Operator: single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJob jobs execute on AMD GPU nodes using ROCm builds of PyTorch. Today accelerated training in the platform is NVIDIA-only; this epic extends the supported training paths to AMD hardware.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable PyTorchJob workloads to run with ROCm builds of PyTorch on AMD GPU nodes, for both single-GPU and multi-GPU (multi-node) job topologies.\n- Provide/validate the training images and runtime prerequisites for ROCm jobs admitted through Kueue queueing.\n- Verify end-to-end admission and completion of ROCm training jobs through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota (requires coordination with the Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling work in this strategy — a coordination point, not a dependency).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- PyTorchJob workloads using ROCm run to completion on AMD GPU nodes for both single-GPU and multi-GPU job topologies.\n- Multi-GPU ROCm PyTorchJobs are admitted through Kueue queueing with amd.com/gpu quota accounted, and complete successfully end to end.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the training-operator side; the Kueue quota side is covered by the Distributed Workloads (Kueue) epic for the same HLR.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- **Upstream ROCm build cadence** (strategy open question): PyTorch ROCm image releases are controlled by AMD and upstream communities; misalignment with release trains is handled by pinning or rebuilding.\n- Validation of training on physical AMD Instinct hardware depends on the same unresolved hardware-access precondition noted in the strategy (procurement or partner-lab access) — a schedule risk, not a structural one.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46229,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91f30b115d6e219b","agent_id":"a5586881f516d3574","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"ddb10bd2-dfe0-4c4a-b603-e248ae90a8be","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:07:41.794Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
