{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1c6d70b0-6d0b-49fe-9727-0fcf01240d8c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-916a55979c6fd966","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-_h9vt6_q/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E005.md","content":"# Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu resources\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic extends the platform's queueing layer (Kueue) so that AMD GPU resources (amd.com/gpu) are handled correctly in quota accounting and workload admission: training workloads requesting AMD GPUs are admitted against amd.com/gpu quota with the same all-or-nothing gang semantics as existing accelerated workloads. Today quota handling and GPU resource discovery in the platform are oriented to NVIDIA GPUs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Support amd.com/gpu as a quota-accounted resource in the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n- Ensure single- and multi-GPU workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted only when their full GPU request can be satisfied (all-or-nothing admission for gang-scheduled jobs).\n- Verify quota enforcement for AMD GPU workloads end to end together with the PyTorch ROCm training enablement in this strategy (coordination point, not a dependency).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted against configured quota when available, and queued or denied when the quota is exhausted, with quota accounting matching the configured amd.com/gpu limits.\n- Multi-GPU workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted only when the full GPU request can be satisfied (all-or-nothing gang admission).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the Kueue quota-handling side; the Training Operator side is covered by the PyTorch ROCm training epic for the same HLR.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- End-to-end verification requires AMD GPU nodes in a test cluster — subject to the strategy's unresolved hardware-access precondition (schedule risk, not a structural one).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46862,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91f30b115d6e219b","agent_id":"a5586881f516d3574","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"f5e54748-1451-4b25-b22e-d5385868a9a3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:07:49.691Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
