{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1ef1c9124001cb2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: whether vLLM serving on AMD Instinct accelerators reaches functional and performance parity with the productized CUDA builds for our supported model set. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware and produces a per-model report with functional pass/fail results, performance measurements against the CUDA baseline, and a go/no-go recommendation that defines the productization scope. The platform currently ships only CUDA runtime builds and has no first-hand parity data, so this campaign is the gate for all serving productization work in this strategy.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Define the validation plan: enumerate the supported model set and the functional and performance parity criteria to be measured for each model.\n34\t- Obtain execution access to physical AMD Instinct GPU nodes (procurement or partner-lab access — see Risks).\n35\t- Serve every model in the supported model set with the upstream vLLM ROCm runtime on AMD Instinct hardware.\n36\t- Record functional results (correct inference behavior vs the CUDA baseline) and performance measurements (throughput and latency) per model.\n37\t- Produce a validation report with a per-model go/no-go recommendation and the resulting productization scope.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A validation plan exists that enumerates the supported model set and defines the functional and performance parity criteria measured for each model.\n42\t- Every model in the supported model set has been served with the vLLM ROCm runtime on physical AMD Instinct hardware and has a recorded functional pass/fail result against the CUDA baseline.\n43\t- Every model in the supported model set has recorded performance measurements (throughput and latency) on AMD Instinct hardware alongside comparable CUDA-baseline numbers.\n44\t- A validation report is published with a per-model go/no-go recommendation that defines the productization scope for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization — fully covered by this epic.\n49\t\n50\t## Risks and Notes\n51\t\n52\t- **Hardware access is unresolved** (strategy open question): dedicated AMD Instinct nodes require procurement or partner-lab access. This is an externally-controlled availability precondition — the epic's deliverable is the validated report; securing access is effort within the epic, but the access being granted is not a condition the deliverable itself produces.\n53\t- **Upstream ROCm image cadence** is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; the campaign consumes upstream ROCm builds and may need to re-run against newer images.\n54\t- The campaign also exercises KServe InferenceService deployment behavior on AMD GPU nodes; findings feed the serving runtime productization scope.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89b736dd626a2092","agent_id":"a2ada6d3756784f07","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"e402b130-4aad-493a-ba69-b62daf876dcd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:10:20.094Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1ef1c9124001cb2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
