uding the required signed attestations for release.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the cleared models — this epic provides the build-pipeline half of that productization (work-product-type split from the runtime productization work; the two run in parallel by rule, coupled only through the runtime epic's build-pipeline-green acceptance criterion).\n49\t\n50\t## Risks and Notes\n51\t\n52\t- The ROCm image's base layers come from AMD's published ROCm images; upstream base-image cadence may require pipeline input updates (fix-and-retry, not a structural change).\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89b736dd626a2092","agent_id":"a2ada6d3756784f07","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"bc64da28-050f-4230-a8dd-cab3cfb7113a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:10:24.149Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a99d7674a3ccee51","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
