{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc584c2458b319d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu resources\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu resources\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic extends the platform's queueing layer (Kueue) so that AMD GPU resources (amd.com/gpu) are handled correctly in quota accounting and workload admission: training workloads requesting AMD GPUs are admitted against amd.com/gpu quota with the same all-or-nothing gang semantics as existing accelerated workloads. Today quota handling and GPU resource discovery in the platform are oriented to NVIDIA GPUs.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Support amd.com/gpu as a quota-accounted resource in the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n38\t- Ensure single- and multi-GPU workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted only when their full GPU request can be satisfied (all-or-nothing admission for gang-scheduled jobs).\n39\t- Verify quota enforcement for AMD GPU workloads end to end together with the PyTorch ROCm training enablement in this strategy (coordination point, not a dependency).\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- Workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted against configured quota when available, and queued or denied when the quota is exhausted, with quota accounting matching the configured amd.com/gpu limits.\n44\t- Multi-GPU workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted only when the full GPU request can be satisfied (all-or-nothing gang admission).\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the Kueue quota-handling side; the Training Operator side is covered by the PyTorch ROCm training epic for the same HLR.\n49\t\n50\t## Risks and Notes\n51\t\n52\t- End-to-end verification requires AMD GPU nodes in a test cluster — subject to the strategy's unresolved hardware-access precondition (schedule risk, not a structural one).\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89b736dd626a2092","agent_id":"a2ada6d3756784f07","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"bd9a8a3a-94bd-47d9-95e4-56e123408810","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:10:28.009Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc584c2458b319d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
