ue.\n49\t- Configuring amd.com/gpu quota in the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Documentation states the supported AMD Instinct hardware and the GPU driver prerequisites for serving and training.\n54\t- Documentation lists the validated model set for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime, matching the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n55\t- Documentation covers PyTorch training on ROCm through Kueue, including amd.com/gpu quota configuration guidance.\n56\t- All documented claims are technically reviewed against the shipped implementation (serving runtime, training enablement, and quota handling as delivered).\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list — fully covered by this epic. This epic's priority (P1) is derived from the strategy's overall priority (Major) per the docs-authoring priority rule, not from HLR-4's P2 label.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89b736dd626a2092","agent_id":"a2ada6d3756784f07","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"998d9b17-789f-4e2b-bec1-0255540f83ef","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:10:29.035Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2b1ced403a7967f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
