{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d479c012c725f03","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the validation campaign clears fewer models than expected\n15\t    or returns a no-go, rewrite the productization scope to the cleared subset (or\n16\t    remove productization entirely on a full no-go) and rescope the support statement\n17\t    accordingly.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic delivers a supported, productized vLLM serving runtime built for AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm), covering the models the validation campaign clears. Today only CUDA (NVIDIA) builds of the vLLM runtime are productized; ROCm builds exist upstream but are neither shipped nor supported. This epic turns the cleared subset of the supported model set into a shipped, supported runtime for the platform.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Build and release a ROCm variant of the vLLM serving runtime image in the existing midstream vLLM repository and release pipeline, scoped to the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n44\t- Provide the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime definitions that expose the ROCm runtime variant for AMD GPU nodes.\n45\t- Verify KServe InferenceService deployment with the ROCm runtime (KServe itself requires no code change — it is validated as a passive component by the same team).\n46\t- Track upstream vLLM ROCm releases and pin to compatible upstream image versions per platform release (upstream cadence risk, see Risks).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- A ROCm build of the vLLM serving runtime is produced and released through the platform release pipeline, scoped to the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n51\t- The ROCm runtime image builds green in the Konflux build pipeline (the build-pipeline onboarding for this image runs in parallel with this epic; its coupling is enforced by this acceptance criterion, not by a dependency between the two work items).\n52\t- Every model cleared by the validation campaign deploys and serves correctly via a KServe InferenceService using the ROCm runtime on AMD GPU nodes.\n53\t- The runtime ships with a support statement identifying the cleared model set and the AMD hardware it is validated on.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the models the validation campaign clears — covered by this epic together with the Konflux build-pipeline work for the ROCm image (a work-product-type split: runtime productization vs. build-pipeline onboarding).\n58\t\n59\t## Risks and Notes\n60\t\n61\t- **Upstream ROCm build cadence** (strategy open question): whether AMD's runtime image releases align with our release trains is outside our control. If cadence misaligns, the runtime pins to or rebuilds from the nearest compatible upstream release — fix-and-retry, not a structural change.\n62\t- The scope of this epic is rewritten (not merely trimmed) by the validation campaign outcome: the cleared model set defines what is productized and what the support statement covers.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b28cc7b159116b11","agent_id":"aa6fa2a184da3964e","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"f8136eb1-13c7-435e-81dd-dd38bdbe3c9f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:15:49.547Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d479c012c725f03","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
