{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-981055bb6d515884","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training enablement for PyTorchJob workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training enablement for PyTorchJob workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic enables PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) for workloads run through the platform's Training Operator: single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJob jobs execute on AMD GPU nodes using ROCm builds of PyTorch. Today accelerated training in the platform is NVIDIA-only; this epic extends the supported training paths to AMD hardware.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Enable PyTorchJob workloads to run with ROCm builds of PyTorch on AMD GPU nodes, for both single-GPU and multi-GPU (multi-node) job topologies.\n38\t- Provide/validate the training images and runtime prerequisites for ROCm jobs admitted through Kueue queueing.\n39\t- Verify end-to-end admission and completion of ROCm training jobs through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota (requires coordination with the Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling work in this strategy — a coordination point, not a dependency).\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- PyTorchJob workloads using ROCm run to completion on AMD GPU nodes for both single-GPU and multi-GPU job topologies.\n44\t- Multi-GPU ROCm PyTorchJobs are admitted through Kueue queueing with amd.com/gpu quota accounted, and complete successfully end to end.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the training-operator side; the Kueue quota side is covered by the Distributed Workloads (Kueue) epic for the same HLR.\n49\t\n50\t## Risks and Notes\n51\t\n52\t- **Upstream ROCm build cadence** (strategy open question): PyTorch ROCm image releases are controlled by AMD and upstream communities; misalignment with release trains is handled by pinning or rebuilding.\n53\t- Validation of training on physical AMD Instinct hardware depends on the same unresolved hardware-access precondition noted in the strategy (procurement or partner-lab access) — a schedule risk, not a structural one.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b28cc7b159116b11","agent_id":"aa6fa2a184da3964e","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"e42e9255-9807-4915-9a36-d0934fb39c7a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:15:53.658Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-981055bb6d515884","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
