MD GPU nodes.\n51\t- The validated model list for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime, as cleared by the validation campaign.\n52\t- Configuring vLLM ROCm serving on AMD GPU nodes (runtime selection via ServingRuntime).\n53\t- Running PyTorch training on ROCm: single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJob jobs admitted through Kueue.\n54\t- Configuring amd.com/gpu quota in the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Documentation states the supported AMD Instinct hardware and the GPU driver prerequisites for serving and training.\n59\t- Documentation lists the validated model set for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime, matching the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n60\t- Documentation covers PyTorch training on ROCm through Kueue, including amd.com/gpu quota configuration guidance.\n61\t- All documented claims are technically reviewed against the shipped implementation (serving runtime, training enablement, and quota handling as delivered).\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list — fully covered by this epic. This epic's priority (P1) is derived from the strategy's overall priority (Major) per the docs-authoring priority rule, not from HLR-4's P2 label.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b28cc7b159116b11","agent_id":"aa6fa2a184da3964e","session_id":"985c5314-dfa6-4bcb-a27c-c01e92aa4111","uuid":"62c657f8-c466-4511-8511-533b51e67311","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:15:58.091Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a89ea8c6a6b62e0b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
